#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:1
msgid "Provably Safe Kernels (preview)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:3
msgid "Preview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:5
msgid ""
"Compile-time Lean 4 verification (`#[verify(...)]` and `cuda-oxide/oxide-"
"proofs-preview/`) is in preview. It covers a validated subset of "
"`PostMem2Reg` integer, shared-memory, barrier, 2-CTA cluster, and Blackwell "
"`tcgen05` / `TMEM` MIR through the pinned Lean `v4.33.1` toolchain. Kernels "
"outside that subset fail closed at compile time, and attribute syntax and "
"supported operations may change between releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:8
msgid "On a CPU, **Safe Rust** means your program has zero undefined behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:9
msgid "No out-of-bounds memory accesses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:10
msgid "No data races between threads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:11
msgid "No dangling pointers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:13
msgid ""
"Notice what Safe Rust does *not* mean: it does not prove **functional "
"correctness** (that your math formula is right). Writing `a[i] - b[i]` when "
"you meant `a[i] + b[i]` is a logic bug, but it is still 100% memory-safe "
"Rust."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:15
msgid ""
"On a GPU, thousands of threads run the same kernel function at once, and the "
"Rust borrow checker cannot reason about thread coordinates or barriers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:16
msgid ""
"**What Rust types already cover**: [Safe Kernels Using Rust's Type System]"
"(the-safety-model.md) proves one-thread-per-element writes with disjoint "
"slices, and [Bounds Checks](bounds-checks.md) hoists row and column checks "
"with matrix views."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:17
msgid ""
"**Where Rust types stop**: When 256 threads share an on-chip tile across "
"barriers, the borrow checker cannot tell if two threads collide or if a "
"barrier sits inside an `if` branch. Without compile-time verification, those "
"kernels require `unsafe` blocks or unchecked indexing flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:18
msgid ""
"**How we make them provably safe**: The `#[verify(...)]` attribute pairs "
"Rust's type system with compile-time **Lean 4** safety proofs, giving you "
"**Provably Safe SIMT** across shared memory, barriers, and async hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:20
msgid "Three GPU safety hazards proved at compile time by the verify attribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:25
msgid ""
"The three GPU safety bugs caught at compile time: out-of-bounds indexing, "
"same-phase shared-memory data races, and divergent barriers."
msgstr ""

