#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:47
msgid "2. How It Works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:49
msgid ""
"Verification splits the work between compile time and launch time so GPU "
"threads pay zero runtime cost:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:50
msgid ""
"**Before launch on the CPU**: The host checks buffer sizes and launch "
"dimensions once per kernel call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:51
msgid ""
"**At compile time in Lean 4**: Right after variables are promoted to SSA "
"registers (and before loops are unrolled), the compiler translates the "
"kernel line by line into Lean 4, proves every safety rule, and deletes the "
"proven bounds checks before generating PTX."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:53
msgid "Specify and Verify pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:58
msgid ""
"The compiler pauses in memory before loop unrolling, proves the kernel safe "
"in Lean 4, erases the proven bounds checks, and resumes lowering to PTX."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:61
msgid "Compile Time vs. Runtime"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:63
msgid ""
"Almost all of the safety checking happens once when you build the kernel. "
"Only the few numbers that do not exist until runtime (like dynamic slice "
"lengths) are checked on the CPU right before launch, leaving the GPU threads "
"completely free of extra checks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:65
msgid "**Proved once at compile time (Lean 4)**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:66
msgid ""
"Every global slice, shared-memory array, barrier array, and Tensor Memory "
"index stays in bounds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:67
msgid ""
"Shared-memory and mutable-slice writes never collide across threads in the "
"same phase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:68
msgid ""
"Block and cluster barriers are reached uniformly by all participating "
"threads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:69
msgid ""
"Async DMA copies, producer-consumer ring buffers, 2-CTA cluster ranks, and "
"Tensor Memory lifecycles happen in the right order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:70
msgid "**Checked once per launch (Host CPU)**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:71
msgid "Block and cluster dimensions match what the kernel declared."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:72
msgid ""
"Runtime buffer sizes satisfy the contract's length rules (for example, "
"inputs are at least as long as the output)."
