#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:106
msgid "How the Compiler Translates Your Kernel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:108
msgid ""
"cuda-oxide translates the kernel instruction by instruction before loop "
"unrolling (while loops are still small and compact):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:109
msgid ""
"**Index math and branches** (adds, shifts, masks, loop counters, and `if` "
"checks) are copied one-for-one into Lean 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:110
msgid ""
"**Floating-point math is ignored**, because float values cannot change which "
"memory slot a thread touches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:111
msgid ""
"**Barriers and async hardware ops** (block syncs, cluster syncs, hardware "
"barriers, DMA copies, work-stealing, and Tensor Memory) are tracked in a "
"small control-flow state machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:112
msgid ""
"**Lean 4 does all the proving**: it turns every memory access and thread "
"pair into plain integer math, checks the hardware ordering rules, and only "
"lets the compiler delete a bounds check once the proof succeeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:114
msgid "Trusted Computing Base"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:116
msgid ""
"Lean 4 checks every proof from scratch and rejects anything that leaves a "
"gap or adds custom assumptions. Everything outside that proof check is part "
"of the **Trusted Computing Base (TCB)**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:117
msgid ""
"**MIR import and SSA promotion**: Lowering Rust into compiler IR and turning "
"stack variables into SSA registers (`--device-debug` skips SSA promotion and "
"is rejected on `#[verify]` modules; pass `--lineinfo` for source-line info "
"instead)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:118
msgid ""
"**The Lean transcriber**: Copying basic blocks and control-flow ops into "
"Lean 4, and stopping immediately if it sees an unsupported instruction or "
"attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:119
msgid ""
"**Downstream lowering**: Deleting proven bounds checks, unrolling loops, and "
"generating LLVM IR and PTX after verification passes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:120
msgid ""
"**Host launch checks and CUDA runtime**: Checking block sizes and buffer "
"lengths on the CPU before launching the kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:124
msgid "3. Reading Verification Errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:126
msgid ""
"When a kernel has a safety bug, compilation stops before PTX is generated. "
"You will see one of two kinds of Lean 4 errors depending on what went wrong:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:128
msgid "Bounds and Data-Race Bugs (Arithmetic Counterexample)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:130
msgid ""
"If an index can walk out of bounds or two threads can collide on the same "
"shared-memory slot (for example, writing `a[idx + 1]` under `if idx < "
"c.len()`, forgetting `if lane == 0`, or dropping a barrier between a write "
"and a read), Lean's integer solver prints a counterexample:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:132
msgid ""
"error: omega could not prove the goal:\n"
"a possible counterexample may satisfy the constraints\n"
"  0 ≤ c ≤ 255\n"
"  a - 256*b - c ≥ 1\n"
"  256*b + c - e ≥ -1\n"
"  a - e ≤ 0\n"
"  ...\n"
"where\n"
"  a := ↑(hvc_512.sliceLen 2)   -- length of parameter 2 (output c)\n"
"  b := ↑hvc_511.bx             -- blockIdx.x\n"
"  c := ↑hvc_511.tx             -- threadIdx.x (0..255)\n"
"  e := ↑(hvc_512.sliceLen 0)   -- length of parameter 0 (input a)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:147
msgid "How to read that output in three quick steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:148
msgid "**Start with the `where` legend at the bottom**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:149
msgid ""
"`sliceLen 0`, `sliceLen 1`, `sliceLen 2` are your slice parameters in "
"function order (`a`, `b`, `c`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:150
msgid ""
"`bx` and `tx` are the block and thread coordinates (`256 * b + c` is the "
"global thread index `idx`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:151
msgid ""
"Any `/ 18446744073709551616` terms are `2^64` from 64-bit `usize` wraparound "
"checks; you can ignore them unless your index math itself overflows 64 bits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:152
msgid "**Read the constraints with those names**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:153
msgid "`a - (256*b + c) >= 1` means the thread passed `idx < c.len()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:154
msgid "`a - e <= 0` means the host launch check `a.len() >= c.len()` holds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:155
msgid ""
"`(256*b + c) - e >= -1` means `idx + 1 >= a.len()`, so `a[idx + 1]` walks "
"off the end of `a`!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:156
msgid ""
"**Plug in a tiny test case**: If both `a` and `c` have length 10, thread 9 "
"passes `9 < 10` and reads `a[9 + 1] = a[10]`, which is out of bounds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:158
msgid "Barrier, Ring, and Tensor Memory Bugs (State-Machine Failure)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:160
msgid ""
"If a barrier sits inside a divergent `if`, a ring producer forgets to wait "
"on its empty barrier, or a Tensor Memory op runs out of order, Lean's "
"control-flow state machine returns `false` instead of `true` and names the "
"check that failed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:162
msgid ""
"error: Application type mismatch: The argument\n"
"  rfl\n"
"... is expected to have type\n"
"  checkTmemLifecycleWith controlFlowCfg cfgStateMap = true\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:169
msgid ""
"`checkUniformBarriersWith ... = true` failing means a block sync, cluster "
"sync, or cyclic ring barrier is not reached cleanly on all active paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:170
msgid ""
"`checkTmemLifecycleWith ... = true` failing means an async proxy fence, "
"barrier wait, full-warp allocation/free, or Tensor Memory column bound was "
"violated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:171
msgid ""
"Run `cargo oxide lean-export <target>` at any time to inspect the generated "
"Lean file alongside your MIR blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:175
msgid "4. Walkthroughs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:177
msgid "Example 1: 1D Vector Addition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:179
msgid ""
"In `safe_vecadd`, each thread checks `c.get_mut(idx)` (`idx < c.len()`) and "
"then reads `a[idx_raw]` and `b[idx_raw]`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:181
msgid ""
"#[launch_contract(\n"
"    domain = 1,\n"
"    block = (256, 1, 1),\n"
"    requires = (a.len() >= c.len(), b.len() >= c.len()),\n"
")]\n"
"#[verify(\n"
"    no_oob_idx(a, b, c),\n"
"    disjoint_writes(c),\n"
"    writes_all_elems(c),\n"
")]\n"
"#[kernel]\n"
"pub fn vecadd(a: &[f32], b: &[f32], mut c: DisjointSlice<f32>) {\n"
"    let idx = thread::index_1d();\n"
"    let idx_raw = idx.get();\n"
"    if let Some(c_elem) = c.get_mut(idx) {\n"
"        *c_elem = a[idx_raw] + b[idx_raw];\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:202
msgid "What happens when you build:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:203
msgid "The host contract guarantees `a` and `b` are at least as long as `c`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:204
msgid ""
"Lean 4 proves that any thread inside `if let Some(c_elem)` is also in bounds "
"for `a` and `b`, and deletes those bounds checks before PTX lowering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:205
msgid ""
"Because `#[verify]` proves `no_oob_idx(c)` and `disjoint_writes(c)` across "
"all GPU threads, you can also write the exact same kernel using plain `c: "
"&mut [f32]` and ordinary slice indexing (with all three bounds checks "
"`a[idx]`, `b[idx]`, and `c[idx]` elided):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:207
msgid ""
"#[launch_contract(\n"
"    domain = 1,\n"
"    block = (256, 1, 1),\n"
"    requires = (a.len() >= c.len(), b.len() >= c.len()),\n"
")]\n"
"#[verify(no_oob_idx(a, b, c), disjoint_writes(c), writes_all_elems(c))]\n"
"#[kernel]\n"
"pub fn vecadd_mut_slice(a: &[f32], b: &[f32], c: &mut [f32]) {\n"
"    let idx = (thread::blockIdx_x() as usize) * (thread::blockDim_x() as "
"usize)\n"
"        + (thread::threadIdx_x() as usize);\n"
"    if idx < c.len() {\n"
"        c[idx] = a[idx] + b[idx];\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

