#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:232
msgid "Example 2: 2D Tiled Matrix Multiply (Shared Memory + Barriers)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:234
msgid ""
"In a 2D tiled matrix multiply (`safe_gemm_views`), a 16x16 block of 256 "
"threads cooperates in two phases separated by a barrier:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:235
msgid ""
"**Phase 0 (Stage)**: Each thread `(tx, ty)` writes one float into shared "
"memory at its own slot (`ty * 16 + tx`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:236
msgid ""
"**Barrier**: All 256 threads wait at `sync_threads()` until both shared "
"tiles are full."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:237
msgid ""
"**Phase 1 (Scan)**: Each thread loops 16 times (`i = 0..16`), reading across "
"row `ty` of tile A and down column `tx` of tile B."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:239
msgid "Phased shared memory verification across sync_threads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:244
msgid ""
"Phase 0 writes one unique slot per thread. After the barrier wall, Phase 1 "
"only reads. Keeping writes and cross-thread reads in separate phases "
"prevents data races."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:247
msgid ""
"Because Lean 4 proves bounds, race freedom, and uniform barriers at compile "
"time:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:248
msgid ""
"**Zero `unsafe` blocks with matrix views**: Adding "
"`#[verify(no_oob_idx(TILE_A, TILE_B), no_data_race(TILE_A, TILE_B), "
"uniform_barriers)]` proves both phases of shared-memory access and removes "
"all 4 shared-memory bounds checks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:249
msgid ""
"**Plain slice indexing without wrapper views**: Even without matrix view "
"types, `sgemm_tiled_raw` is 100% safe Rust and removes all 6 bounds checks "
"(2 on global slices `a` and `b`, plus 4 on shared tiles `TILE_A` and "
"`TILE_B`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:251
msgid ""
"#[kernel(launch_context = lc)]\n"
"#[launch_bounds(256)]\n"
"#[launch_contract(domain = 2, coordinates = u32, block = (16, 16, 1),\n"
"    requires = (k >= 1, a.len() >= m * k, b.len() >= k * n, c.len() >= m * "
"n))]\n"
"#[verify(\n"
"    no_oob_idx(a, b, TILE_A, TILE_B),\n"
"    no_data_race(TILE_A, TILE_B),\n"
"    uniform_barriers,\n"
")]\n"
"pub fn sgemm_tiled_raw(\n"
"    m: u32,\n"
"    n: Uniform<u32>,\n"
"    k: u32,\n"
"    alpha: f32,\n"
"    a: &[f32],\n"
"    b: &[f32],\n"
"    beta: f32,\n"
"    mut c: DisjointSlice<f32, RuntimeRowMajorTiles<1, 1>>,\n"
") {\n"
"    static mut TILE_A: SharedArray<f32, 256> = SharedArray::UNINIT;\n"
"    static mut TILE_B: SharedArray<f32, 256> = SharedArray::UNINIT;\n"
"    // ...\n"
"    while tile < num_tiles {\n"
"        // ...\n"
"        // Phase 0 (Lean-verified bounds and disjoint per-thread slot):\n"
"        {\n"
"            TILE_A[smem_idx] = a_value;\n"
"            TILE_B[smem_idx] = b_value;\n"
"        }\n"
"\n"
"        thread::sync_threads();\n"
"\n"
"        // Phase 1 (Lean-verified bounds and barrier separation):\n"
"        {\n"
"            let mut i = 0usize;\n"
"            while i < TILE as usize {\n"
"                sum += TILE_A[ty as usize * 16 + i] * TILE_B[i * 16 + tx as "
"usize];\n"
"                i += 1;\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"\n"
"        thread::sync_threads();\n"
"        tile = tile.wrapping_add(1);\n"
"    }\n"
"    // ...\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

