#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:315
msgid "Example 3: Warp & 2-Phase Block Reduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:317
msgid ""
"In a 256-thread block reduction, 8 warps of 32 threads sum 256 elements in "
"two phases using an 8-element shared array (`WARP_SUMS`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:318
msgid ""
"**Phase 0 (Warp Leader Stage)**: Every thread reduces across its 32-lane "
"warp. Guarded by `if lane == 0`, only lane 0 of each warp writes its warp "
"sum to `WARP_SUMS[tid / 32]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:319
msgid "**Barrier**: All 256 threads wait at `sync_threads()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:320
msgid ""
"**Phase 1 (Block Scan)**: Each thread scans `w = 0..8` across `WARP_SUMS[w]` "
"to accumulate the 256-thread block sum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:322
msgid "Leader-guarded warp and block reduction in shared memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:327
msgid ""
"In Phase 0, only lane 0 of each warp writes `WARP_SUMS[tid / 32]`, so each "
"warp slot has a single writer. After the barrier, Phase 1 only reads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:330
msgid ""
"Notice that the kernel uses the **exact same three verification clauses** as "
"2D tiled GEMM (`no_oob_idx`, `no_data_race`, `uniform_barriers`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:332
msgid ""
"#[kernel(launch_context = lc)]\n"
"#[launch_bounds(256)]\n"
"#[launch_contract(\n"
"    domain = 1,\n"
"    coordinates = u32,\n"
"    block = (256, 1, 1),\n"
"    requires = (data.len() >= out.len()),\n"
")]\n"
"#[verify(\n"
"    no_oob_idx(WARP_SUMS),\n"
"    no_data_race(WARP_SUMS),\n"
"    uniform_barriers,\n"
")]\n"
"pub fn block_reduce_sum(data: &[f32], mut out: DisjointSlice<f32>) {\n"
"    static mut WARP_SUMS: SharedArray<f32, 8> = SharedArray::UNINIT;\n"
"\n"
"    let idx = thread::index_1d();\n"
"    let gid = idx.get();\n"
"    let tid = thread::threadIdx_x() as usize;\n"
"    let lane = warp::lane_id();\n"
"\n"
"    let val = if gid < data.len() { data[gid] } else { 0.0 };\n"
"    let warp_sum = warp::reduce_sum_f32(val);\n"
"\n"
"    // Phase 0 (Lean-verified bounds and single leader writer per warp):\n"
"    if lane == 0 {\n"
"        WARP_SUMS[tid / 32] = warp_sum;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    thread::sync_threads();\n"
"\n"
"    // Phase 1 (Lean-verified bounds and barrier separation):\n"
"    let mut block_sum = 0.0f32;\n"
"    let mut w = 0usize;\n"
"    while w < 8 {\n"
"        block_sum += WARP_SUMS[w];\n"
"        w += 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    if let Some(out_elem) = out.get_mut(idx) {\n"
"        *out_elem = block_sum;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:378
msgid "How Lean 4 proves this kernel (and what happens if you make a mistake):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:379
msgid ""
"**Phase 0 bounds**: Because `tid < 256`, `tid / 32` is at most 7, which is "
"strictly below 8."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:380
msgid ""
"**Phase 0 race freedom**: The exporter sees that the write happens inside "
"`if lane == 0`. Lean 4 proves that two threads with `lane == 0` and the same "
"warp index `tid / 32` must be the exact same thread. If you forget `if lane "
"== 0`, Lean 4 rejects the build with a counterexample (threads 0 and 1 both "
"write slot 0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:381
msgid ""
"**Phase 1 bounds and barrier separation**: The loop bound `w < 8` stays "
"inside the 8-element array, and `sync_threads()` separates Phase 0 writes "
"from Phase 1 reads, erasing both shared-memory bounds checks before PTX "
"lowering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:383
msgid "Inspect both exported reduction kernels or run them on the GPU with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:385
msgid ""
"$ cargo oxide lean-export safe_warp_reduce\n"
"$ cargo oxide run safe_warp_reduce\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:392
msgid "Example 4: Sub-Warp Bitwise Splits & Multi-Buffer Staging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:394
msgid ""
"High-throughput kernels often split a 256-thread block into **16 sub-warps "
"of 16 lanes** using bit shifts and masks (`tid >> 4` and `tid & 15`) and "
"stage data across **three shared-memory buffers** of different sizes over "
"three barrier phases:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:395
msgid ""
"**Phase 0 (Guarded & packed stage)**: The first 64 threads each write one "
"scale into the 64-float buffer and four packed activations into the 256-"
"float buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:396
msgid ""
"**Phase 1 (Sub-warp scan & leader write)**: Every thread scans across its "
"sub-warp's slice, reduces across 16 lanes with warp shuffles, and lets lane "
"0 of each sub-warp write one output into the 16-float buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:397
msgid ""
"**Phase 2 (Epilogue read)**: After a second barrier, the first 16 threads "
"read the 16 sub-warp results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:399
msgid ""
"Three-phase sub-warp bit-split and multi-buffer staging in shared memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:404
msgid ""
"Two barriers separate guarded packing in Phase 0, sub-warp scanning and "
"leader writes in Phase 1, and the final epilogue read in Phase 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:407
msgid ""
"#[kernel(launch_context = lc)]\n"
"#[launch_bounds(256)]\n"
"#[launch_contract(\n"
"    domain = 1,\n"
"    coordinates = u32,\n"
"    block = (256, 1, 1),\n"
"    requires = (data.len() >= out.len()),\n"
")]\n"
"#[verify(\n"
"    no_oob_idx(S_X_DIRECT, S_XS_DIRECT, S_ACT_DIRECT),\n"
"    no_data_race(S_X_DIRECT, S_XS_DIRECT, S_ACT_DIRECT),\n"
"    uniform_barriers,\n"
")]\n"
"pub fn multibuf_subwarp_stage(data: &[f32], mut out: DisjointSlice<f32>) {\n"
"    static mut S_X_DIRECT: SharedArray<f32, 256> = SharedArray::UNINIT;\n"
"    static mut S_XS_DIRECT: SharedArray<f32, 64> = SharedArray::UNINIT;\n"
"    static mut S_ACT_DIRECT: SharedArray<f32, 16> = SharedArray::UNINIT;\n"
"\n"
"    let idx = thread::index_1d();\n"
"    let gid = idx.get();\n"
"    let tid = thread::threadIdx_x() as usize;\n"
"    let m_local = tid >> 4;\n"
"    let k_lane = tid & 15;\n"
"    let base_val = if gid < data.len() { data[gid] } else { 0.0 };\n"
"\n"
"    // Phase 0 (Lean-verified under `if tid < 64`):\n"
"    if tid < 64 {\n"
"        S_XS_DIRECT[tid] = 0.5f32;\n"
"        let mut w = 0usize;\n"
"        while w < 4 {\n"
"            S_X_DIRECT[tid * 4 + w] = base_val;\n"
"            w += 1;\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    thread::sync_threads();\n"
"\n"
"    // Phase 1 (Lean-verified sub-warp lane scan + `if k_lane == 0` leader "
"write):\n"
"    let mut sum = 0.0f32;\n"
"    let mut g = 0usize;\n"
"    while g < 4 {\n"
"        sum += S_X_DIRECT[k_lane * 16 + g] * S_XS_DIRECT[k_lane * 4 + g];\n"
"        g += 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    sum += warp::shuffle_xor_f32(sum, 8);\n"
"    sum += warp::shuffle_xor_f32(sum, 4);\n"
"    sum += warp::shuffle_xor_f32(sum, 2);\n"
"    sum += warp::shuffle_xor_f32(sum, 1);\n"
"\n"
"    if k_lane == 0 {\n"
"        S_ACT_DIRECT[m_local] = sum;\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    thread::sync_threads();\n"
"\n"
"    // Phase 2 (Lean-verified under `if tid < 16` after second barrier):\n"
"    let mut final_val = sum;\n"
"    if tid < 16 {\n"
"        final_val = S_ACT_DIRECT[tid];\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    if let Some(out_elem) = out.get_mut(idx) {\n"
"        *out_elem = final_val;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:475
msgid ""
"How Lean 4 proves all three buffers and removes all 6 shared-memory bounds "
"checks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:476
msgid ""
"**Phase 0 bounds and disjoint chunks**: Inside `if tid < 64`, each active "
"thread stays below 64 on the scale buffer and owns its own 4-float chunk "
"(`tid * 4 + w < 256`) on the activation buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:477
msgid ""
"**Phase 1 sub-warp bounds and single writer**: Masking with `tid & 15` keeps "
"every lane index below 16 across all 256 threads, while `if k_lane == 0` "
"ensures only one leader thread writes each sub-warp slot (`tid >> 4 < 16`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:478
msgid ""
"**Phase 2 barrier separation**: Two block-wide barriers separate Phase 0 "
"writes, Phase 1 reads/writes, and Phase 2 reads. Widening the guard from 64 "
"to 128 or dropping the second barrier is rejected at compile time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:480
msgid "Inspect both sub-warp kernels or run them on the GPU with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:482
msgid ""
"$ cargo oxide lean-export safe_subwarp_stage\n"
"$ cargo oxide run safe_subwarp_stage\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:489
msgid "Example 5: Asynchronous TMA Bulk Copy & Barrier Ordering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:491
msgid ""
"On Hopper and Blackwell GPUs, global-to-shared copies run asynchronously on "
"the **Tensor Memory Accelerator (TMA)** engine while threads coordinate "
"through a shared-memory hardware barrier instead of a full block sync:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:492
msgid ""
"**Producer (thread 0)**: Sets the expected byte count on the barrier and "
"kicks off the 2D TMA copy into shared memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:493
msgid ""
"**Consumer wait (all 256 threads)**: Spins on the barrier until both the "
"thread arrival and the byte transfer finish."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:494
msgid ""
"**Consumer read (all 256 threads)**: Reads from the shared tile with zero "
"`unsafe` blocks in the kernel body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:496
msgid "Asynchronous 2D TMA bulk copy and hardware barrier handoff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:501
msgid ""
"Thread 0 arms the byte count and launches the 2D TMA transfer; all 256 "
"threads wait on the barrier before reading the staged tile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:504
msgid ""
"#[kernel(launch_context = lc)]\n"
"#[launch_bounds(256)]\n"
"#[launch_contract(\n"
"    domain = 1,\n"
"    coordinates = u32,\n"
"    block = (256, 1, 1),\n"
")]\n"
"#[verify(\n"
"    no_oob_idx(TILE),\n"
"    no_data_race(TILE),\n"
"    uniform_barriers,\n"
")]\n"
"pub fn async_copy_stage(\n"
"    #[grid_constant] tensor_map: &TmaDescriptor,\n"
"    mut out: DisjointSlice<f32>,\n"
"    tile_x: i32,\n"
"    tile_y: i32,\n"
") {\n"
"    static mut TILE: SharedArray<f32, 4096, 128> = SharedArray::UNINIT;\n"
"    static mut BAR: Barrier = Barrier::UNINIT;\n"
"\n"
"    let idx = thread::index_1d();\n"
"    let tid = thread::threadIdx_x() as usize;\n"
"\n"
"    if tid == 0 {\n"
"        mbarrier_init(&raw mut BAR, 1);\n"
"        fence_proxy_async_shared_cta();\n"
"    }\n"
"    thread::sync_threads();\n"
"\n"
"    // Producer (thread 0 kicks off the 16 KiB TMA copy):\n"
"    if tid == 0 {\n"
"        let _ = mbarrier_arrive_expect_tx(&raw const BAR, 1, 16384);\n"
"        cp_async_bulk_tensor_2d_g2s_cta(\n"
"            &raw mut TILE as *mut u8,\n"
"            tensor_map,\n"
"            tile_x,\n"
"            tile_y,\n"
"            &raw mut BAR,\n"
"        );\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    // All 256 threads wait until the TMA transfer completes:\n"
"    while !mbarrier_try_wait_parity(&raw const BAR, 0) {}\n"
"\n"
"    // Safe read with bounds check removed:\n"
"    let val = TILE[tid];\n"
"    if let Some(out_elem) = out.get_mut(idx) {\n"
"        *out_elem = val;\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:558
msgid "How Lean 4 checks this handoff:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:559
msgid ""
"**Single producer**: Because the TMA launch sits inside `if tid == 0`, only "
"thread 0 starts the shared-memory write."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:560
msgid ""
"**Transfer size fits**: Lean 4 checks that the 16,384-byte transfer (4,096 "
"floats) fits inside the shared array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:561
msgid ""
"**Wait before read**: Lean 4 checks that the barrier is initialized, fenced, "
"armed with the expected byte count, and awaited on every path before any "
"thread reads the tile. Skipping the wait or forgetting to arm the byte count "
"stops compilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:563
msgid "Inspect the exported Lean proof or run the TMA copy on the GPU with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:565
msgid ""
"$ cargo oxide lean-export safe_async_copy\n"
"$ cargo oxide run safe_async_copy\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:572
msgid "Example 6: Blackwell Tensor Cores & Tensor Memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:574
msgid ""
"On datacenter Blackwell GPUs (such as NVIDIA B200), 5th-generation Tensor "
"Cores accumulate into dynamically allocated **Tensor Memory (TMEM)** instead "
"of regular registers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:575
msgid ""
"**Allocation (warp 0)**: Warp 0 allocates 128 columns of Tensor Memory and "
"stores the base address in shared memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:576
msgid ""
"**TMA + Tensor Core issue (thread 0)**: Thread 0 loads the input tiles via "
"TMA, issues the matrix multiply into Tensor Memory, and commits completion "
"to a barrier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:577
msgid ""
"**Epilogue & free (all 4 warps)**: After waiting on the barrier, each warp "
"reads its own 32-lane slice out of Tensor Memory, syncs across the block, "
"and lets warp 0 free the 128 columns, all with zero `unsafe` blocks in the "
"kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:579
msgid "Blackwell Tensor Core and Tensor Memory lifecycle verification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:584
msgid ""
"Warp 0 allocates 128 Tensor Memory columns, thread 0 issues and commits the "
"Tensor Core multiply, each warp reads its own 32-lane slice, and warp 0 "
"frees the columns after a block sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:587
msgid ""
"#[kernel(launch_context = lc)]\n"
"#[launch_bounds(128)]\n"
"#[launch_contract(\n"
"    domain = 1,\n"
"    coordinates = u32,\n"
"    block = (128, 1, 1),\n"
")]\n"
"#[verify(\n"
"    no_oob_idx(SMEM_A, SMEM_B, TMEM_ADDR),\n"
"    no_data_race(SMEM_A, SMEM_B, TMEM_ADDR),\n"
"    uniform_barriers,\n"
"    tmem_lifecycle\n"
")]\n"
"pub fn tcgen05_matmul_verified(\n"
"    #[grid_constant] a_tmap: &TmaDescriptor,\n"
"    #[grid_constant] b_tmap: &TmaDescriptor,\n"
"    mut out: DisjointSlice<f32, LinearTiles<128>>,\n"
"    tile_x: i32,\n"
"    tile_y: i32,\n"
") {\n"
"    static mut SMEM_A: SharedArray<u8, 4096, 128> = SharedArray::UNINIT;\n"
"    static mut SMEM_B: SharedArray<u8, 4096, 128> = SharedArray::UNINIT;\n"
"    static mut TMEM_ADDR: SharedArray<u32, 1, 4> = SharedArray::UNINIT;\n"
"    static mut TMA_A_BAR: Barrier = Barrier::UNINIT;\n"
"    static mut TMA_B_BAR: Barrier = Barrier::UNINIT;\n"
"    static mut MMA_BAR: Barrier = Barrier::UNINIT;\n"
"\n"
"    let idx32 = thread::index_1d_u32(lc);\n"
"    let tid = thread::threadIdx_x() as usize;\n"
"    let warp_id = warp::warp_id();\n"
"\n"
"    if tid == 0 {\n"
"        mbarrier_init(&raw mut TMA_A_BAR, 1);\n"
"        mbarrier_init(&raw mut TMA_B_BAR, 1);\n"
"        mbarrier_init(&raw mut MMA_BAR, 1);\n"
"        fence_proxy_async_shared_cta();\n"
"    }\n"
"    thread::sync_threads();\n"
"\n"
"    if warp_id == 0 {\n"
"        tcgen05_alloc(&raw mut TMEM_ADDR[0], 128);\n"
"    }\n"
"    thread::sync_threads();\n"
"    let tmem_addr = TMEM_ADDR[0];\n"
"    // ... TMA loads, Tensor Core MMA + commit, barrier wait, and TMEM "
"load ...\n"
"    thread::sync_threads();\n"
"    if warp_id == 0 {\n"
"        tcgen05_dealloc(tmem_addr, 128);\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

