#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:649
msgid "Example 7: Warp-Specialized Ring Buffers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:651
msgid ""
"Fast persistent kernels rarely stop the whole block at a single barrier. "
"Instead, they split warps by role: one **producer warp** streams tiles into "
"a multi-stage ring buffer, while **consumer warps** compute on earlier "
"stages at the same time, coordinating through arrays of barriers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:653
msgid "Warp-specialized 4-stage producer and consumer ring buffer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:658
msgid ""
"Warp 4 fills ring slots ahead of Warps 0..3; full-barrier and empty-barrier "
"arrays keep each slot's writes and reads ordered across laps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:661
msgid ""
"What Lean 4 checks in the warp-ring example (erasing all 9 bounds checks "
"with zero `unsafe` blocks):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:662
msgid ""
"**Ring wrap stays in bounds**: Whether you advance the stage counter with an "
"`if` wraparound, `% 4`, or `& 3`, Lean 4 proves the stage index stays below "
"4 on every lap. An off-by-one wrap like `== 5` is caught at compile time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:663
msgid ""
"**Matching barrier and data slots**: Waiting on slot `s` of the full-barrier "
"array only unlocks slot `s` of the ring buffer. Waiting on slot `s` and "
"accidentally reading `(s + 1) & 3` is rejected as a data race."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:664
msgid ""
"**No overwriting live data**: If the producer loop forgets to wait on the "
"empty barrier before refilling a slot on the next lap, Lean 4 rejects the "
"loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:666
msgid "$ cargo oxide run safe_warp_ring\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:672
msgid "Example 8: 2-CTA Clusters & Hardware Work-Stealing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:674
msgid ""
"On Blackwell, two neighboring thread blocks can team up as a **2-CTA "
"cluster** to share tiles across Distributed Shared Memory (DSMEM) and pull "
"work dynamically from hardware **Cluster Launch Control (CLC)**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:676
msgid "Two-CTA cluster DSMEM exchange and hardware work-stealing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:681
msgid ""
"Two partner blocks synchronize across the cluster before reading each "
"other's shared memory, while hardware work-stealing delivers the next tile "
"into a verified 16-byte buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:684
msgid ""
"**Safe peer rank**: In a 2-block cluster, your block rank is 0 or 1, so "
"flipping the low bit (`my_rank ^ 1`) always points to your valid partner "
"block. Lean 4 proves that peer rank is in bounds, and rejects bugs like "
"`my_rank + 1` (which walks out of bounds on block 1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:685
msgid ""
"**Cluster-wide syncs**: A local block sync only waits for your own block. "
"Lean 4 checks that you run a full cluster sync before reading your partner "
"block's shared memory or freeing shared 2-CTA Tensor Memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:686
msgid ""
"**Work-stealing mailbox**: Hardware work-stealing writes a 16-byte response "
"asynchronously. Lean 4 checks that the response buffer is at least 16 bytes "
"wide and that threads wait on its completion barrier before reading the "
"stolen tile ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:688
msgid "$ cargo oxide run safe_cluster_clc\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:694
msgid "Example 9: Speed-of-Light Blackwell GEMM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:696
msgid ""
"The final example puts every piece together in a full production FP16/BF16 "
"matrix multiply for NVIDIA B200 (6 warps per block across a 2-block cluster):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:697
msgid ""
"**Warp 4 (Producer + Work-Stealing)**: Streams A and B tiles into a 7-stage, "
"224 KiB shared-memory ring using 2-CTA multicast TMA, overlaps hardware work-"
"stealing for the next tile, and posts tile coordinates to a 4-slot mailbox."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:698
msgid ""
"**Warp 5 (2-CTA Tensor Cores)**: Issues cooperative 2-CTA Tensor Core "
"instructions into two alternating 256-column halves of a 512-column Tensor "
"Memory buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:699
msgid ""
"**Warps 0..3 (Epilogue)**: Unload Tensor Memory into registers, release the "
"Tensor Memory stage early so the next tile can start, shuffle BF16 pairs "
"across lanes, and write 128-bit stores to global memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:701
msgid "Verified 2-CTA Blackwell GEMM pipeline in safe_gemm_sol_final"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:706
msgid ""
"Lean 4 verifies all seven shared-memory and barrier arrays, partner CTA "
"ranks, work-stealing responses, and 512-column Tensor Memory stages at "
"compile time, erasing all 27 bounds checks with zero register spills."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-safety/verified-kernels.md:709
msgid ""
"All 224 KiB of shared memory, all 11 hardware barriers, cross-block DSMEM "
"signaling, hardware work-stealing, and all 512 columns of Tensor Memory run "
"without `unsafe` (leaving only one 4-line `unsafe` block at the very end for "
"the 128-bit vectorized global output store on dynamically stolen tile "
"coordinates)."
msgstr ""

